<p>These Driver App Terms govern access to Koast's chauffeur software and related support provided by Krujim Inc, doing business as Koast. They apply to chauffeurs and other people authorized to use a driver account. Our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains personal-information practices across Koast products.</p>

<h2 id="relationship">1. Your role and other agreements</h2>
<p>The app supports transportation work arranged by the relevant operator. It does not by itself hire you, classify you as an independent contractor, promise work or compensation, or authorize you to provide transportation. Employment, contractor, vehicle, insurance, compensation and transportation-service arrangements are governed by applicable law and your separate agreement with the responsible company. These app terms do not replace those agreements or waive rights that cannot lawfully be waived.</p>
<p>If you also book rides as a passenger, the <a href="/terms/rider/">Rider Terms</a> apply to that activity. An operator's business use of Connect is covered separately by the <a href="/terms/connect/">Connect Terms</a> and any applicable business agreement.</p>

<h2 id="access">2. Authorized access and account security</h2>
<p>Use only your own authorized account and the functions made available to your role. Provide accurate information and keep sign-in credentials, codes and access links secure. Do not share an account, impersonate another chauffeur, bypass permissions or access another organization's records. Notify your operator or Koast promptly if you suspect unauthorized access. Access may depend on the operator relationship and eligibility information recorded for your account.</p>

<h2 id="safe-use">3. Safe and accurate use</h2>
<p>Follow applicable laws and the responsible operator's lawful instructions. Review assigned-trip details and keep availability and trip statuses accurate. Do not interact with the app while doing so would distract you from safe driving. Stop safely before using controls that require attention. Maps, traffic, ETAs, flight updates, notifications and AI suggestions can be incomplete or delayed; use professional judgment and contact dispatch when a critical detail needs confirmation.</p>
<p>The app is not an emergency service or a guarantee that dispatch or another person is watching your location, messages or recordings. For an emergency, contact emergency services directly and notify dispatch when safe.</p>

<h2 id="passenger-data">4. Passenger and business information</h2>
<p>Use passenger contact details, addresses, trip instructions and operator information only for authorized transportation, safety and support purposes. Do not copy or disclose customer lists, retain information for unrelated use, contact passengers for personal or unauthorized marketing purposes, or share access links publicly. Protect information on any device you use and report suspected loss or misuse promptly.</p>
<p>Submit documents and other content only when you are entitled to provide them. Koast and the responsible operator may process that content to operate, secure and support the service, as explained in the Privacy Policy and applicable operator arrangements.</p>

<h2 id="permissions">5. Location, recordings and connected features</h2>
<p>Location-enabled features may collect precise coordinates for dispatch and ride tracking, including garage positioning around accepted work. The Privacy Policy explains the relevant uses, recipients and controls. Turning tracking or device permissions off may affect availability, dispatch and tracking features. Contact your operator about any work requirements; these terms do not create undisclosed tracking obligations.</p>
<p>Recording is optional where the feature is available. Obtain required participant consent and follow the recording notices and applicable law before recording. Authorized Koast owner review can occur without a filed incident report. Do not record secretly or assume a recording is being monitored in real time. Optional Calendar, microphone, camera and notification features have their own permissions; grant only those you choose to use.</p>

<h2 id="acceptable-use">6. Acceptable use and app rights</h2>
<p>Koast permits you to use the app for its intended, authorized purposes while access remains available. Koast and its licensors retain rights in their software and branding; you retain your rights in content you lawfully provide. Do not misuse the service, introduce malicious code, attempt unauthorized access, interfere with service or other users, scrape restricted records, or use the app for unlawful, abusive or fraudulent activity.</p>

<h2 id="service-access">7. Service changes and ending access</h2>
<p>Functions and availability may change, and connectivity or third-party services may interrupt access. Keep a practical way to contact dispatch when the app is unavailable. Koast or your authorized operator may restrict access when needed for security, safety, unlawful use or the end of your authorization, subject to applicable law and any governing agreement. Ending app access does not decide your employment status, resolve compensation owed or erase required business records.</p>
<p>For a privacy or deletion request, use the methods in the Privacy Policy. We may need to coordinate with the company responsible for the relevant records.</p>

<h2 id="changes-contact">8. Updates, other agreements and contact</h2>
<p>We identify revisions by date and provide notice of material changes where required. A separately signed agreement governing the same subject controls to the extent of a conflict, subject to applicable law. These app terms do not introduce a separate arbitration requirement, liability cap, indemnity or waiver of mandatory rights.</p>
<p>Questions about access or software: <a href="mailto:reserve@koastride.com">reserve@koastride.com</a>. Questions about an assignment, work relationship or compensation should also be directed to the responsible operator.</p>
